# The API document is hashed, not just read.
#
# Its sha256 is the "fingerprint" printed on every API Validation report and
# shown in the document panel, so two machines holding the same document must
# agree on it. Left to git's end-of-line normalisation, a Windows checkout and
# the Linux server produced different fingerprints for the same file — which
# makes the one thing the fingerprint exists for, identifying a version,
# useless. -text keeps the bytes exactly as committed.
assets/api-validation/*.yaml -text
